# The magic weapons, as modifiers applied to a real weapon rather
# than as items of their own. PCGen demands that anything typed
# Weapon declare Melee or Ranged, and none of these is one weapon:
# a Flame Tongue is any melee weapon and a Berserker Axe is one of
# three axes. Each carries the PRETYPE its own first line states.

Adamantine Armor	KEY:Adamantine Armor	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Uncommon	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	!PRETYPE:1,Hide Armor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.209	SPROP:Armor (Any Medium or Heavy, Except Hide Armor), Uncommon. This suit of armor is reinforced with adamantine, one of the hardest substances in existence. While you’re wearing it, any Critical Hit against you becomes a normal hit.
+1 Ammunition	KEY:+1 Ammunition	TYPE:ALL.MagicWeapon.Uncommon	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Ammunition	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.209	BONUS:WEAPON|TOHIT|1	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE|1	SPROP:Weapon (Any Ammunition), Uncommon (+1), Rare (+2),. or Very Rare (+3) You have a bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this piece of magic ammunition. The bonus is determined by the rarity of the ammunition. Once it hits a target, the ammunition is no longer magical. This ammunition is typically found or sold in quantities of ten or twenty pieces. Ten pieces of this ammunition are equivalent in value to a potion of the same rarity.
+2 Ammunition	KEY:+2 Ammunition	TYPE:ALL.MagicWeapon.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Ammunition	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.209	BONUS:WEAPON|TOHIT|2	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE|2	SPROP:Weapon (Any Ammunition), Uncommon (+1), Rare (+2),. or Very Rare (+3) You have a bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this piece of magic ammunition. The bonus is determined by the rarity of the ammunition. Once it hits a target, the ammunition is no longer magical. This ammunition is typically found or sold in quantities of ten or twenty pieces. Ten pieces of this ammunition are equivalent in value to a potion of the same rarity.
+3 Ammunition	KEY:+3 Ammunition	TYPE:ALL.MagicWeapon.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Ammunition	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.209	BONUS:WEAPON|TOHIT|3	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE|3	SPROP:Weapon (Any Ammunition), Uncommon (+1), Rare (+2),. or Very Rare (+3) You have a bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this piece of magic ammunition. The bonus is determined by the rarity of the ammunition. Once it hits a target, the ammunition is no longer magical. This ammunition is typically found or sold in quantities of ten or twenty pieces. Ten pieces of this ammunition are equivalent in value to a potion of the same rarity.
Ammunition of Slaying	KEY:Ammunition of Slaying	TYPE:ALL.MagicWeapon.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Ammunition	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.209	SPROP:Weapon (Any Ammunition), Very Rare. This magic ammunition is meant to slay creatures of a particular type, which the GM chooses or determines randomly by rolling on the table below. If a creature of that type takes damage from the ammunition, the creature makes a DC 17 Constitution saving throw, taking an extra 6d10 Force damage on a failed save or half as much extra damage on a successful one. After dealing its extra damage to a creature, the ammunition becomes nonmagical. 01–10 Aberrations 51–60 Fey 11–15 Beasts 61–70 Fiends 16–20 Celestials 71–75 Giants 21–25 Constructs 76–80 Monstrosities 26–35 Dragons 81–85 Oozes 36–45 Elementals 86–90 Plants 46–50 Humanoids 91–00 Undead
Animated Shield	KEY:Animated Shield	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Shield	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.209	SPROP:Armor (Shield), Very Rare (Requires Attunement). While holding this Shield, you can take a Bonus Action to cause it to animate. The Shield leaps into the air and hovers in your space to protect you as if you were wielding it, leaving your hands free. The Shield remains animate for 1 minute, until you take a Bonus Action to end this effect, or until you die or have the Incapacitated condition, at which point the Shield falls to the ground or into your hand if you have one free.
+1 Armor	KEY:+1 Armor	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (+1), Very Rare (+2), or Legendary (+3) You have a bonus to Armor Class while wearing this armor. The bonus is determined by its rarity.
+2 Armor	KEY:+2 Armor	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|2	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (+1), Very Rare (+2), or Legendary (+3) You have a bonus to Armor Class while wearing this armor. The bonus is determined by its rarity.
+3 Armor	KEY:+3 Armor	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Legendary	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|3	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (+1), Very Rare (+2), or Legendary (+3) You have a bonus to Armor Class while wearing this armor. The bonus is determined by its rarity.
Armor of Invulnerability	KEY:Armor of Invulnerability	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Legendary	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Plate Armor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Plate Armor), Legendary (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage while you wear this armor. Metal Shell. You can take a Magic action to give yourself Immunity to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage for 10 minutes or until you are no longer wearing the armor. Once this property is used, it can’t be used again until the next dawn.
Armor of Resistance (Acid)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Acid)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Acid damage.
Armor of Resistance (Necrotic)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Necrotic)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Necrotic damage.
Armor of Resistance (Cold)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Cold)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Cold damage.
Armor of Resistance (Poison)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Poison)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Poison damage.
Armor of Resistance (Fire)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Fire)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Fire damage.
Armor of Resistance (Psychic)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Psychic)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Psychic damage.
Armor of Resistance (Force)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Force)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Force damage.
Armor of Resistance (Radiant)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Radiant)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Radiant damage.
Armor of Resistance (Lightning)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Lightning)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Lightning damage.
Armor of Resistance (Thunder)	KEY:Armor of Resistance (Thunder)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.210	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. This armor gives Resistance to Thunder damage.
Armor of Vulnerability	KEY:Armor of Vulnerability	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.211	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement) While wearing this armor, you have Resistance to one of the following damage types: Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing. The GM chooses the type or determines it randomly. Curse. This armor is cursed, a fact that is revealed only when the Identify spell is cast on the armor or you attune to it. Attuning to the armor curses you until you are targeted by a Remove Curse spell or similar magic; removing the armor fails to end the curse. While cursed, you have Vulnerability to two of the three damage types associated with the armor (not the one to which it grants Resistance).
Arrow-Catching Shield	KEY:Arrow-Catching Shield	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Shield	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.211	SPROP:Armor (Shield), Rare (Requires Attunement). You gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class against ranged attack rolls while you wield this Shield. This bonus is in addition to the Shield’s normal bonus to AC. Whenever an attacker makes a ranged attack roll against a target within 5 feet of you, you can take a Reaction to become the target of the attack instead.
Berserker Axe	KEY:Berserker Axe	TYPE:ALL.MagicWeapon.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Battleaxe,Greataxe,Halberd	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.213	BONUS:WEAPON|TOHIT|1	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE|1	BONUS:HP|CURRENTMAX|TL*1	SPROP:Weapon (Battleaxe, Greataxe, or Halberd), Rare (Requires Attunement) You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, while you are attuned to this weapon, your Hit Point maximum increases by 1 for each level you have attained. Curse. This weapon is cursed, and becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. As long as you remain cursed, you are unwilling to part with the weapon, keeping it within reach at all times. You also have Disadvantage on attack rolls with weapons other than this one. Whenever another creature damages you while the weapon is in your possession, you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or go berserk. This berserk state ends when you start your turn and there are no creatures within 60 feet of you that you can see or hear. While berserk, you regard the creature nearest to you that you can see or hear as your enemy. If there are multiple possible creatures, choose one at random. On each of your turns, you must move as close to the creature as possible and take the Attack action, targeting the creature. If you’re unable to get close enough to the creature to attack it with the weapon, your turn ends after you’ve used up all your available movement. If the creature dies or can no longer be seen or heard by you, the next nearest creature that you can see or hear becomes your new target.
Dagger of Venom	KEY:Dagger of Venom	TYPE:ALL.MagicWeapon.Rare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Dagger	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.216	BONUS:WEAPON|TOHIT|1	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE|1	SPROP:Weapon (Dagger), Rare. You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. You can take a Bonus Action to magically coat the blade with poison. The poison remains for 1 minute or until an attack using this weapon hits a creature. That creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or take 2d10 Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute. The weapon can’t be used this way again until the next dawn.
Dancing Sword	KEY:Dancing Sword	TYPE:ALL.MagicWeapon.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Greatsword,Longsword,Rapier,Scimitar,Shortsword	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.217	SPROP:Weapon (Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Very Rare (Requires Attunement). You can take a Bonus Action to toss this magic weapon into the air. When you do so, the weapon begins to hover, flies up to 30 feet, and attacks one creature of your choice within 5 feet of itself. The weapon uses your attack roll and adds your ability modifier to damage rolls. While the weapon hovers, you can take a Bonus Action to cause it to fly up to 30 feet to another spot within 30 feet of you. As part of the same Bonus Action, you can cause the weapon to attack one creature within 5 feet of the weapon. After the hovering weapon attacks for the fourth time, it flies back to you and tries to return to your hand. If you have no hand free, the weapon falls to the ground in your space. If the weapon has no unobstructed path to you, it moves as close to you as it can and then falls to the ground. It also ceases to hover if you grasp it or are more than 30 feet away from it.
Defender	KEY:Defender	TYPE:ALL.MagicWeapon.Legendary	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Melee	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.218	BONUS:WEAPON|TOHIT|3	BONUS:WEAPON|DAMAGE|3	SPROP:Weapon (Any Melee Weapon), Legendary (Requires Attunement) You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. The first time you attack with the weapon on each of your turns, you can transfer some or all of the weapon’s bonus to your Armor Class. For example, you could reduce the bonus to your attack rolls and damage rolls to +1 and gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class. The adjusted bonuses remain in effect until the start of your next turn, although you must hold the weapon to gain a bonus to AC from it.
Demon Armor	KEY:Demon Armor	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,LightArmor,MediumArmor,HeavyArmor	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.218	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|1	SPROP:Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Very Rare (Requires Attunement) While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class, and you know Abyssal. In addition, the armor’s clawed gauntlets allow your Unarmed Strikes to deal 1d8 Slashing damage instead of the usual Bludgeoning damage, and you gain a +1 bonus to the attack and damage rolls of your Unarmed Strikes. Curse. Once you don this cursed armor, you can’t doff it unless you are targeted by a Remove Curse spell or similar magic. While wearing the armor, you have Disadvantage on attack rolls against demons and on saving throws against their spells and special abilities.
Dragon Scale Mail (Black)	KEY:Dragon Scale Mail (Black)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Scale Mail	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.218	SPROP:Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare (Requires Attunement). Dragon Scale Mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them. Other times, hunters carefully preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, Dragon Scale Mail is highly valued. Additionally, you can focus your senses as a Magic action to discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of yourself that is of the same type as the armor. This action can’t be used again until the next dawn. This armor is made from the scales of a Black dragon, so it gives Resistance to Acid damage and detects dragons of that kind.
Dragon Scale Mail (Gold)	KEY:Dragon Scale Mail (Gold)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Scale Mail	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.218	SPROP:Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare (Requires Attunement). Dragon Scale Mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them. Other times, hunters carefully preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, Dragon Scale Mail is highly valued. Additionally, you can focus your senses as a Magic action to discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of yourself that is of the same type as the armor. This action can’t be used again until the next dawn. This armor is made from the scales of a Gold dragon, so it gives Resistance to Fire damage and detects dragons of that kind.
Dragon Scale Mail (Blue)	KEY:Dragon Scale Mail (Blue)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Scale Mail	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.218	SPROP:Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare (Requires Attunement). Dragon Scale Mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them. Other times, hunters carefully preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, Dragon Scale Mail is highly valued. Additionally, you can focus your senses as a Magic action to discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of yourself that is of the same type as the armor. This action can’t be used again until the next dawn. This armor is made from the scales of a Blue dragon, so it gives Resistance to Lightning damage and detects dragons of that kind.
Dragon Scale Mail (Green)	KEY:Dragon Scale Mail (Green)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Scale Mail	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.218	SPROP:Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare (Requires Attunement). Dragon Scale Mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them. Other times, hunters carefully preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, Dragon Scale Mail is highly valued. Additionally, you can focus your senses as a Magic action to discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of yourself that is of the same type as the armor. This action can’t be used again until the next dawn. This armor is made from the scales of a Green dragon, so it gives Resistance to Poison damage and detects dragons of that kind.
Dragon Scale Mail (Brass)	KEY:Dragon Scale Mail (Brass)	TYPE:ALL.MagicArmor.VeryRare	VISIBLE:QUALIFY	PRETYPE:1,Scale Mail	SOURCEPAGE:SRD 5.2.1, p.218	SPROP:Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare (Requires Attunement). Dragon Scale Mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them. Other times, hunters carefully preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, Dragon Scale Mail is highly valued. Additionally, you can focus your senses as a Magic action to discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of yourself that is of the same type as the armor. This action can’t be used again until the next dawn. This armor is made from the scales of a Brass dragon, so it gives Resistance to Fire damage and detects dragons of that kind.
